ition file for `terms.readiness`.\n- The test inspects the first model request's prompt (`requests[0].body[\"messages\"][0][\"content\"]`) and asserts that it contains:\n  - the full requirement text (`REQUIREMENT`),\n  - the definition text (`SECRET_DEFINITION_TEXT`),\n  - `fn ready()` and `fn ready_test()`,\n  - the prompt template text.\n- It asserts that the old rationale is not sent to the model.\n- The evidence record's `inputs` also contain the `terms.readiness` definition.\n\nTogether these cover the example's expected outcome: the initial prompt carries the complete requirement, both cited functions and the required definition. The unit test adds the finer points: smallest enclosing item, transitive terms, direct-only references, and generated-evidence exclusion.\n\nNo gaps or FIXMEs apply to this example. The `FIXME(#125)` in the CLI fixture relates to a different requirement (acknowledged gaps).",
